# Provider binaries and local state — a reusable module commits neither; the
# consuming root module's lock and state govern. The module's OWN lock file is
# the one exception: a consumer's init ignores a child module's lock entirely,
# while committing it pins the provider CI resolves — without it, an AWS
# provider release can redden the blocking terraform jobs on an unrelated PR.
**/.terraform/*
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
crash.log
